Moybyte's changes to dash v0.5.13.5 (native/moy_sh/UPSTREAM.md).

dash as a session of the kernel's shell rather than a process of a Unix:

- Every writable global is a field of the session's record, struct
  moy_sh_globals (native/moy_sh/moy_sh_g.h): a definition becomes
  `#define name (moy_sh_g->name)`, an aggregate `(*moy_sh_g->name)`, so the
  objects keep no .data or .bss and a fork is a snapshot of one arena. The
  types such fields need move from .c files into headers (struct ifsregion,
  struct stdin_state, struct stack_block, MINSIZE); output's `output` is
  `outputf`; tags and members a macro would rewrite are renamed (parsefile_s,
  stdin_state_s, heredoc_s, a job's jctl); stackmark's members are mark_*.
- The POSIX calls go to native/moy_sh/moy_sh_posix.h (included after the
  system headers): there is no fork, exec, wait, signal or tty. forkshell
  takes the child's body as a function (moy_sh_fork runs it to its end);
  evalsubshell, evalpipe and evalbackcmd pass theirs; shellexec and the
  default command case call moy_sh_exec; vforkexec, tryexec and the forked
  here-document writer go (a pipe buffer holds the whole document); waitproc
  waits through moy_sh_wait, nonblocking as wait3 was, and a waiting `wait`
  blocks there; a blocking wait names its job (moy_sh_foreground) so Ctrl-C
  reaches it; process groups and the tty go.
- Input is pushed: the parser raises EXMORE (error.h) where it would read past
  what the face sent, which the session answers with MOY_SH_MORE; the end of
  that text is marked (input_eof). dotrap polls the host for Ctrl-C first.
- main() and the profile go (the session starts dash, native/moy_sh/moy_sh.c);
  cmdloop and setprompt are public. find_builtin falls back to the shell's own
  table (moy_sh_find_builtin). The environment is not imported, PATH is /bin,
  setlocale and putenv go, mail checking, times and dash_errno go.
- Signal names with no entry (NULL) are skipped.
- Headers a chip's C library lacks and nothing uses go (sys/ioctl.h,
  sys/mman.h, arpa/inet.h: htonl is moy_sh_posix.h's).

